00:14:54.440 --> 00:14:56.740
So a service catalog is
a special interest group

00:14:56.740 --> 00:14:58.690
that's part of Kubernetes.

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:02.230
And so we're doing work there
in the Kubernetes community

00:15:02.230 --> 00:15:04.480
to add that capability
to Kubernetes.

00:15:04.480 --> 00:15:06.640
And service mesh is
something that Louis

00:15:06.640 --> 00:15:11.250
will get into depth on, and
it's another open source project

00:15:11.250 --> 00:15:14.230
that we're engaged in.

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:15.820
It's actually called Istio.

00:15:15.820 --> 00:15:19.750
But we'll get to the
URLs for that later.

00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:24.935
So what these do-- we talked
about what the broker does.

00:15:24.935 --> 00:15:27.520
It's a core service abstraction.

00:15:27.520 --> 00:15:31.990
And the catalog
basically provides

00:15:31.990 --> 00:15:34.370
environment-specific
help to sort of get

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:36.310
consumption of services
to be something

00:15:36.310 --> 00:15:38.170
that is very natural
in an environment,

00:15:38.170 --> 00:15:39.490
in this case, Kubernetes.

00:15:39.490 --> 00:15:42.550
And the mesh is for
traffic management

00:15:42.550 --> 00:15:47.330
and inter-service
policy controls.

